On 10/26/07, Alex Martini <alexjm@umich.edu> wrote:
>
>  Also, is {togyno} valid?

No, {y} can't be used in fu'ivla.

> Jbofi'e
> prefers {togrno}, and I seem to remember {r} being the typical rafsi
> glue for making fu'ivla.

{r} is used to join the initial CCVC-, CVCC- or CVC- with the
remaining C.... part of a type-3 fu'ivla. The three possible patterns
of type-3 fu'ivla are: CCVC-r-C..., CVCC-r-C..., CVC-r-C...

If -r- can't be used because the preceding or following consonant
is an r, use -n-. If -n- can't be used, use -l-.

